# PerformIQ ML Service — configuration reference
# The FastAPI service has no .env file; all runtime options are passed via CLI.
# Copy and adapt the commands below as needed.

# ── Start command ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# From inside ml-service/, with the venv active:
#
#   uvicorn main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
#
# Or, from the project root using the helper script:
#
#   cd ml-service && venv\Scripts\uvicorn.exe main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
#
# Change --host / --port to suit your environment.
# In production, run behind a reverse-proxy (nginx/Caddy) and do NOT bind to 0.0.0.0
# unless the host is properly firewalled.

# ── Model file ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The service loads ml-service/performiq_model.joblib at startup.
# If you retrain the model, replace that file and restart the service.

# ── Health check ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/health  →  {"status": "ok", "model_loaded": true}
